-- title:
--   Local box of a preimage order under an injective map
-- statement:
--   Fix rationals $a_1,b_1,c,d$, a finite index type $n$ with decidable equality, and an injective homomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebras $\tau : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_n(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$. Let $O$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d]$ that is an order in the sense of the project predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d]$, and it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ which is assumed to be exactly the preimage of the matrix order, in the pointwise form: for all $x$, $x \in R$ if and only if $\tau(x)_{il} \in O$ for all $i,l \in n$. Let $w$ be a height-one prime of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ and let $x$ belong to $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_w$, where $\mathbb{Q}_w$ is the $w$-adic completion. For a lattice $\Lambda$, [`Submodule.localBox`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) $\Lambda\, w$ denotes the additive subgroup of the base change generated by the elements $z \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_w$. The assertion is that $x$ lies in the local box of $R$ at $w$ if and only if, for all $i,l \in n$, the image of $x$ under the $\mathbb{Q}_w$-base change (`LinearMap.rTensor`) of the $\mathbb{Q}$-linear map $x \mapsto \tau(x)_{il}$ lies in the local box of $O$ at $w$.
--
--   This is the statement that forming the $w$-adic box of a lattice commutes with taking the preimage of a matrix order under an injective embedding of quaternion algebras, i.e. $(\tau^{-1}M_n(O))_w = \tau_w^{-1}(M_n(O_w))$ place by place. It is used in the construction of a ring homomorphism into a product of matrix algebras characterising membership in local boxes, in the treatment of maximal orders in rational quaternion algebras.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_mem_localBox_iff_forall_rTensor_entryLinearMap_comp_mem_localBox.lean

